<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB2-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB2-002" ;
  triage:title "Stale Completion ACK by receiver step in both edited SKILL.md files, unreconciled with the sprint's own task-close model" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BB2-QA1-1789243200 (Final verdict FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1439#issuecomment-5648494400, 2026-09-12T20:28:31Z), reviewed at 67a6a3fe4. .claude/skills/graph-orchestration/SKILL.md:544-551 and .claude/skills/codex-orchestration/SKILL.md:235-242 -- both files' Required Message Sequence section still lists a generic 4-step protocol ending in a distinct 'Completion ACK by receiver' step, unchanged by this sprint. But every dispatch template (the two this sprint edited, plus the four pre-existing ones) now treats `atm task close {{ task_id }} completed ...` as the terminal, self-sufficient completion signal -- no template instructs the lead/assigner to send back a separate ack, and D5's own new prose says the lead 'reads that report and proceeds,' not that it acks it. Confirmed independently by both req-qa and arch-qa (req-qa finding 4, arch-qa ARCH-002). A future team-lead session reading only the stale section could conclude a manual ack/close step is still owed on the mirror task, contradicting D5." ;
